# h3-spark2 — the same H3 engine, launched ON spark-2, for scene-parallel
# sequence rendering (one engine per Spark, independent clips each).
#
# vLLM-Omni cannot split one render across nodes; this is clip-level
# parallelism, which needs nothing from the fabric except reachability.
# Everything inherits from h3.env — image, fp8, timeouts, mods — with one
# difference: the bind address. spark-2's engine listens on its fabric IP,
# which only spark-1 can reach over the DAC cable. Nothing touches the LAN;
# the console and the sequencer reach it through spark-1 (the hermes tunnel
# forwards 18092 -> 192.168.100.2:8091 via the spark-1 hop).
#
# Run FROM spark-2:   rack up h3-spark2
# Weights must be synced first (rsync of local/MiniMax-H3/FL2VA — same path).
. recipes/h3.env
SERVE_ARGS+=(--host 192.168.100.2)   # last --host wins over launch-solo's 127.0.0.1
